ible until the call center spikes.`},{theme:`value`,q:`When infrastructure monitoring has worked well, what did it save you — time, risk, or reputation?`,probe:`Capture a concrete win to anchor expansion beyond hosts.`}]},{id:`security`,label:`Security`,focus:`Sensitive workloads, least privilege, and audit-ready evidence`,questions:[{theme:`usage`,q:`Which infrastructure tiers are considered too sensitive for broader instrumentation today?`,probe:`Get Melanie’s boundary early — OpenShift namespaces and mainframe often top the list.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`What evidence do you need before approving agents or runtime visibility in production?`,probe:`Least privilege, data residency, and change control — not feature demos.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`Where do infrastructure gaps create security blind spots you cannot defend in an audit?`,probe:`Unknown hosts and unowned clusters are usually the honest answer.`},{theme:`value`,q:`Where has better runtime visibility already reduced security friction at go-live?`,probe:`If none yet, that’s the partnership opportunity — evidence before the final gate.`}]},{id:`devops`,label:`DevOps`,focus:`Deploy confidence across hybrid platforms`,questions:[{theme:`usage`,q:`Do release teams look at infrastructure health before and after a deploy to EKS/ECS or OpenShift?`,probe:`If not, deploys and infra alerts stay in separate worlds.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`What infrastructure signal do you wish you had during the last bad release?`,probe:`Often dependency impact or node pressure tied to a version.`},{theme:`value`,q:`What would “safe to promote” look like if infrastructure and services shared one picture?`,probe:`Define the gate in their words — then map Dynatrace to it.`}]}]},{id:`cicd`,name:`CI / CD & DevOps`,accent:`cicd`,hotspot:{left:38,top:4,width:24,height:28},summary:`Jenkins, Puppet, and ServiceNow — change, deploy, and ticket flow that rarely share a live production signal.`,personas:[{id:`itops`,label:`IT Operations`,focus:`Change impact and ticket enrichment`,questions:[{theme:`usage`,q:`How do production incidents get linked back to a Jenkins deploy or Puppet change today?`,probe:`Manual correlation is the common pain — and the Dynatrace opportunity.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`Where does “waiting on more detail” show up between ServiceNow and the people who can fix it?`,probe:`Missing context in tickets drives TTR up without anyone owning the gap.`},{theme:`value`,q:`When a change was rolled back quickly, what signal made that decision obvious?`,probe:`Capture that signal so it can become the default, not the exception.`}]},{id:`security`,label:`Security`,focus:`Controlled change and deploy evidence`,questions:[{theme:`usage`,q:`Which deploy or config changes require security sign-off before production?`,probe:`Understand the gate so observability evidence can arrive earlier.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`What worries you most about automated pipeline changes hitting sensitive services?`,probe:`Blast radius and incomplete rollback proof usually dominate.`},{theme:`value`,q:`What proof would make a pipeline change feel safer to approve?`,probe:`Health before/after, ownership, and a clear escalation path.`}]},{id:`devops`,label:`DevOps`,focus:`Pipeline feedback and release quality`,questions:[{theme:`usage`,q:`Where do developers look first when a Jenkins deploy “succeeds” but customers complain?`,probe:`If the answer isn’t production observability, the pipeline is lying by omission.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`What is the biggest delay between commit and confident production validation?`,probe:`Separate that into build time vs. “is it healthy?” time.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`How noisy are deploy-related alerts versus actionable release failures?`,probe:`Noise trains teams to ignore the only signal that matters.`},{theme:`value`,q:`What release metric would you put on a shared scoreboard this quarter?`,probe:`Failed deploy rate, time to detect, or customer-impact minutes.`}]}]},{id:`observability`,name:`Monitoring & Observability`,accent:`observability`,hotspot:{left:63,top:4,width:32,height:30},summary:`Splunk, Prometheus, Grafana, and OpenTelemetry — parallel tools that compete for attention during incidents.`,personas:[{id:`itops`,label:`IT Operations`,focus:`Single pane vs. swivel-chair triage`,questions:[{theme:`usage`,q:`In the last major incident, how many consoles did the bridge open in the first 15 minutes?`,probe:`Count tools out loud — it makes consolidation concrete.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`Where do Prometheus/Grafana alerts disagree with Splunk or Dynatrace?`,probe:`Conflicting truth destroys trust faster than missing data.`},{theme:`value`,q:`Which tool do people actually trust to declare “customer impact has started”?`,probe:`That tool is your political north star for unification.`}]},{id:`security`,label:`Security`,focus:`Signal quality and sensitive log/trace handling`,questions:[{theme:`usage`,q:`Which observability data stores are in scope for security monitoring today?`,probe:`Clarify overlap between SIEM-style use and ops observability.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`What data classes must never land in a shared observability platform without controls?`,probe:`Get constraints explicit before proposing OTel or trace expansion.`},{theme:`value`,q:`Where would correlated runtime + security context shorten an investigation?`,probe:`Vulnerable library in a hot service is the classic example.`}]},{id:`devops`,label:`DevOps`,focus:`Dashboards that drive action, not decoration`,questions:[{theme:`usage`,q:`Which Grafana boards are sacred — and which are abandoned?`,probe:`Abandoned boards reveal where tooling failed adoption.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`How much custom instrumentation toil sits with app teams vs. a platform team?`,probe:`OTel + Dynatrace can reduce duplicate effort if ownership is clear.`},{theme:`value`,q:`What would “one investigative path” change about on-call for your squads?`,probe:`Time-to-insight and fewer handoffs are the outcomes to name.`}]}]},{id:`security`,name:`Security`,accent:`security`,hotspot:{left:8,top:40,width:26,height:22},summary:`Tenable, Synopsys, and unknown runtime risk — where late gates and missing production context collide.`,personas:[{id:`itops`,label:`IT Operations`,focus:`Runtime risk during incidents`,questions:[{theme:`usage`,q:`When an incident smells like a vulnerability exploit, what do ops open first?`,probe:`If scanners and runtime are disconnected, response stalls.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`How often do security findings arrive without a clear production exposure path?`,probe:`Prioritization pain is the opening for runtime context.`},{theme:`value`,q:`What would “this CVE is reachable in prod on these services” change in your next war room?`,probe:`Speed and shared ownership between ops and security.`}]},{id:`security`,label:`Security`,focus:`Melanie’s gate — evidence before go-live`,questions:[{theme:`usage`,q:`Where does Tenable or Synopsys stop — and runtime truth need to begin?`,probe:`Scan results ≠ production exposure.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`What typically causes a late-stage block on monitoring or release initiatives?`,probe:`Listen for process, data, and accountability — not just tools.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`What does “unknown vulnerabilities” mean operationally for this bank?`,probe:`Third-party libs, shadow services, or incomplete inventories.`},{theme:`value`,q:`What success looks like for Security if Dynatrace becomes part of the control story?`,probe:`Earlier involvement, clearer evidence, fewer surprise blocks.`}]},{id:`devops`,label:`DevOps`,focus:`Shift-left without slowing delivery`,questions:[{theme:`usage`,q:`How do app teams hear about Synopsys/Tenable findings today?`,probe:`Ticket dumps vs. in-pipeline feedback changes adoption.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`What security check feels like pure friction versus real protection?`,probe:`Replace friction with runtime-backed prioritization.`},{theme:`value`,q:`If security evidence arrived earlier in the pipeline, what would ship faster?`,probe:`Name a product surface — banking or trading — to keep it real.`}]}]},{id:`applications`,name:`Applications`,accent:`apps`,hotspot:{left:58,top:38,width:36,height:28},summary:`Next.js, Tomcat, and the digital channels — online banking, trading, mobile — where customers feel every gap.`,personas:[{id:`itops`,label:`IT Operations`,focus:`Customer-impact minutes and channel health`,questions:[{theme:`usage`,q:`How do you know online banking or trading is degraded before social and the call center tell you?`,probe:`If you can’t, RUM/DEM is the missing floor on this building.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`Which application failures stay invisible because we only watch hosts?`,probe:`Slow pages, bad deploys, and third-party callbacks are usual suspects.`},{theme:`value`,q:`What does a “good hour” look like for digital channels in measurable terms?`,probe:`Apdex, conversion, error rate, or journey completion — pick one.`}]},{id:`security`,label:`Security`,focus:`Customer-facing attack surface`,questions:[{theme:`usage`,q:`Which customer-facing apps are in scope for runtime application security conversations?`,probe:`Banking and trading should be on that list explicitly.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`What worries you about instrumenting mobile and web journeys?`,probe:`PII in RUM, consent, and third-party scripts.`},{theme:`value`,q:`Where would user-journey context help prove a security incident’s real blast radius?`,probe:`Tie sessions to affected services and data paths.`}]},{id:`devops`,label:`DevOps`,focus:`Frontend + service ownership`,questions:[{theme:`usage`,q:`Who owns Next.js vs. Tomcat health when a release lands — platform or product squads?`,probe:`Unclear ownership = orphaned dashboards.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`What micro-apps or long-tail services are nobody sure still matter?`,probe:`Inventory first — then coverage standards.`},{theme:`value`,q:`What feedback loop would make developers trust production signals the morning after deploy?`,probe:`Automatic problem → owner → deploy link is the pattern.`}]}]},{id:`databases`,name:`Databases`,accent:`data`,hotspot:{left:30,top:52,width:24,height:18},summary:`Microsoft SQL Server and unknown stores — performance and dependency truth behind every transaction.`,personas:[{id:`itops`,label:`IT Operations`,focus:`Query health and dependency impact`,questions:[{theme:`usage`,q:`When SQL Server is slow, how do you know which banking journey is paying the price?`,probe:`Host CPU without service context is the classic trap.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`What unknown data stores scare you most during an incident?`,probe:`Shadow DBs and replicas without owners.`},{theme:`value`,q:`What database win would leadership recognize immediately?`,probe:`Avoided outage, faster batch, or clearer capacity story.`}]},{id:`security`,label:`Security`,focus:`Data sensitivity and access paths`,questions:[{theme:`usage`,q:`Which data stores hold the crown jewels for commercial, private, or investment banking?`,probe:`Prioritize monitoring and access evidence there first.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`What monitoring of databases is blocked by data-handling policy today?`,probe:`Shape the ask around metadata and performance, not row content.`},{theme:`value`,q:`How would clearer service→database topology help audit and incident response?`,probe:`Who touched what, and what customer path depends on it.`}]},{id:`devops`,label:`DevOps`,focus:`Schema/release impact on data tiers`,questions:[{theme:`usage`,q:`Do app teams see slow-query or DB wait evidence after a release?`,probe:`If only DBAs see it, feedback is too late.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`What database change process creates the most production surprise?`,probe:`Migrations, index jobs, or connection pool tweaks.`},{theme:`value`,q:`What would shared DB+app telemetry change about your definition of done?`,probe:`Done = journey healthy, not only deploy green.`}]}]},{id:`hub`,name:`Platform Hub`,accent:`hub`,hotspot:{left:42,top:70,width:18,height:16},summary:`Dynatrace as the hub — where signals should converge for IT Ops, Security, and DevOps together.`,personas:[{id:`itops`,label:`IT Operations`,focus:`Trusted operating picture`,questions:[{theme:`usage`,q:`For which incident types is Dynatrace already the first open tab?`,probe:`Protect and expand those workflows first.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`What keeps Dynatrace from being the system of action during a bridge call?`,probe:`Coverage, trust, or skill — diagnose which.`},{theme:`value`,q:`What operational KPI should this partnership move in 90 days?`,probe:`MTTR, waiting time, or customer-impact minutes.`}]},{id:`security`,label:`Security`,focus:`Platform as control evidence`,questions:[{theme:`usage`,q:`How is Security involved in Dynatrace configuration and data decisions today?`,probe:`Early partnership vs. late veto.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`What would need to be true for Security to sponsor broader runtime visibility?`,probe:`Write it down — that becomes the enablement checklist.`},{theme:`value`,q:`What security outcome should appear on the shared success scorecard?`,probe:`Fewer late blocks, faster vuln triage, or audit-ready evidence.`}]},{id:`devops`,label:`DevOps`,focus:`Platform adoption by builders`,questions:[{theme:`usage`,q:`Which squads already self-serve in Dynatrace without opening a ticket?`,probe:`Those are your champions for the roadmap.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`What makes developers avoid the platform even when it is installed?`,probe:`UX, permissions, or “not my tool” culture.`},{theme:`value`,q:`What developer experience win would prove Dynatrace belongs in the inner loop?`,probe:`Faster root cause after deploy is the usual answer.`}]}]},{id:`edge`,name:`Edge & Unknown`,accent:`edge`,hotspot:{left:58,top:84,width:36,height:12},summary:`SaaS, integrations, edge, and unknown services — the first mile and the unmanaged last mile.`,personas:[{id:`itops`,label:`IT Operations`,focus:`Vendor and edge dependencies`,questions:[{theme:`usage`,q:`When a SaaS or partner integration fails, how do you prove it isn’t “our bank”?`,probe:`Synthetic and dependency views earn their keep here.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`Which unknown services have bitten you in the last two quarters?`,probe:`Start an honest inventory from pain, not CMDB fiction.`},{theme:`value`,q:`What edge or partner SLO would you put on the executive page?`,probe:`Regional experience or partner availability.`}]},{id:`security`,label:`Security`,focus:`Third-party and shadow risk`,questions:[{theme:`usage`,q:`How do you assess third-party integrations that sit on customer journeys?`,probe:`Connect vendor risk to runtime dependency maps.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`What unknown or shadow services are unacceptable from a control perspective?`,probe:`Discovery becomes a security initiative, not only an ops one.`},{theme:`value`,q:`What would a living inventory of edge and SaaS dependencies unlock for Security?`,probe:`Faster reviews and fewer surprises at go-live.`}]},{id:`devops`,label:`DevOps`,focus:`Integration ownership`,questions:[{theme:`usage`,q:`Who owns the health of critical 3rd-party callbacks used by mobile or web?`,probe:`If “the vendor,” you still need a consumer-side signal.`},{theme:`concerns`,q:`Where do integration failures show up late in testing or only in production?`,probe:`Contract tests + production dependency health.`},{theme:`value`,q:`What integration reliability story would product managers fund?`,probe:`Checkout, quote, or funds-transfer paths.`}]}]}];function zd(e){return Rd.find(t=>t.name===e)}var Bd=[{id:`see`,floorLabel:`See it`,title:`See it`,domain:`Coverage`,question:`How much of this technology is monitored?`,distinction:`Do we know what is monitored—and what is not?`,levels:[{score:1,label:`Brand New`,description:`Little or no monitoring; coverage is unknown.`},{score:2,label:`Basic`,description:`Some important production systems are monitored, usually through manual deployment.`},{score:3,label:`Operational`,description:`Most production systems are monitored, and known gaps are documented.`},{score:4,label:`Highly Mature`,description:`Coverage is measured, automated, and built into deployment processes.`}]},{id:`understand`,floorLabel:`Understand it`,title:`Understand it`,domain:`Visibility depth`,question:`When it has a problem, how much can we understand?`,distinction:`Can we only see that it is broken, or can we understand why?`,levels:[{score:1,label:`Brand New`,description:`Basic up/down status or infrastructure metrics only.`},{score:2,label:`Basic`,description:`Technology-specific metrics, logs, alerts, and dashboards are available.`},{score:3,label:`Operational`,description:`Performance, errors, dependencies, changes, and affected services can be identified.`},{score:4,label:`Highly Mature`,description:`Metrics, logs, traces, topology, user impact, and business impact are automatically correlated.`}]},{id:`use`,floorLabel:`Use it`,title:`Use it`,domain:`Operational adoption`,question:`Do teams actually use the monitoring during incidents and daily operations?`,distinction:`Is the platform installed, or is it trusted?`,levels:[{score:1,label:`Brand New`,description:`Teams rarely use it or do not know it exists.`},{score:2,label:`Basic`,description:`A few specialists use it, usually after another tool identifies the problem.`},{score:3,label:`Operational`,description:`Operations and development teams regularly use it for troubleshooting.`},{score:4,label:`Highly Mature`,description:`It is the trusted starting point for incidents, releases, capacity decisions, and service reviews.`}]},{id:`own`,floorLabel:`Own it`,title:`Own it`,domain:`Governance`,question:`Who is responsible for keeping the monitoring useful?`,distinction:`When monitoring becomes incomplete or noisy, who fixes it?`,levels:[{score:1,label:`Brand New`,description:`No clear owner exists.`},{score:2,label:`Basic`,description:`A tool administrator owns the platform, but service teams have limited responsibility.`},{score:3,label:`Operational`,description:`Platform and service teams have defined responsibilities for coverage, alerts, and dashboards.`},{score:4,label:`Highly Mature`,description:`Ownership, standards, reviews, escalation paths, and observability requirements are embedded across teams.`}]},{id:`improve`,floorLabel:`Improve it`,title:`Improve it`,domain:`Outcomes`,question:`Can we prove that monitoring creates better results?`,distinction:`Can we show that monitoring changed an outcome?`,levels:[{score:1,label:`Brand New`,description:`No goals or success measurements exist.`},{score:2,label:`Basic`,description:`Technical metrics are tracked, such as uptime or alert volume.`},{score:3,label:`Operational`,description:`Results such as MTTR, incident frequency, release quality, or availability are measured.`},{score:4,label:`Highly Mature`,description:`Monitoring is continuously improved based on SLOs, customer experience, business impact, and measurable value.`}]}],Vd=()=>({see:0,understand:0,use:0,own:0,improve:0});function Hd(e){return Bd.reduce((t,n)=>t+(e[n.id]||0),0)}function Ud(e){return e<=0?{label:`Not scored`,className:`band-none`}:e<=8?{label:`Brand new`,className:`band-new`}:e<=12?{label:`Basic`,className:`band-basic`}:e<=16?{label:`Operational`,className:`band-ops`}:{label:`Highly mature`,className:`band-mature`}}var Wd=`landscape-health-scores`,Gd=`landscape-health-scores-cleared`;function Kd(){try{localStorage.removeItem(Wd)}catch{}window.dispatchEvent(new Event(Gd))}var qd=[{id:`full`,label:`Full coverage`,note:`Full Dynatrace coverage`},{id:`partial`,label:`Partial coverage`,note:`Partial / limited coverage`},{id:`none`,label:`No coverage`,note:`No coverage — blind spot`},{id:`infra-only`,label:`Infra only`,note:`Infrastructure / host monitoring only`},{id:`apm`,label:`APM / traces`,note:`APM / distributed traces in place`},{id:`rum`,label:`RUM / DEM`,note:`RUM / digital experience covered`},{id:`logs`,label:`Logs connected`,note:`Logs ingested / correlated`